IO-47: restore the groundwater table from a runoff interface file with the right sign

subcatch_getResults() saves the water table elevation as
gw->bottomElev + gw->lowerDepth, but runoff_readFromFile() restored
gw->lowerDepth as Aquifer[].bottomElev - elevation: the negative of the depth,
measured from the aquifer's bottom rather than the subcatchment's own (which
[GROUNDWATER] can override). A USE RUNOFF run reported the water table
mirrored below the aquifer bottom. Subtract gw->bottomElev from the elevation.

Requires: IO-46

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply IO-46_swmm530.patch IO-47_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/runoff.c b/src/legacy/engine/runoff.c
index b28536e..76a3749 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/runoff.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/runoff.c
@@ -471,8 +471,8 @@ void  runoff_readFromFile(void)
             if ( Subcatch[j].area > 0.0 )
                 gw->newFlow = SubcatchResults[SUBCATCH_GW_FLOW] / UCF(FLOW) /
                               Subcatch[j].area;
-            gw->lowerDepth = Aquifer[gw->aquifer].bottomElev -
-                             (SubcatchResults[SUBCATCH_GW_ELEV] / UCF(LENGTH));
+            gw->lowerDepth = SubcatchResults[SUBCATCH_GW_ELEV] / UCF(LENGTH) -
+                             gw->bottomElev;
             gw->theta      = SubcatchResults[SUBCATCH_SOIL_MOIST];
         }
 
